      "widgets_values": [
        "ROOF CUTOUT \u2014 BUILT-IN NODES ONLY\n\n1. Upload roof-source.png in Load Image.\n2. Right-click Load Image > Open in Mask Editor.\n3. Paint MASK over everything to REMOVE: sky, landscape, floor, basin, text and the interiors of all three openings. Leave the canopy, cream rim and side supports unpainted.\n4. Save the mask back to the node, then Run / Queue.\n5. Mask preview: WHITE = removed, BLACK = kept.\n6. Save Image writes an RGBA PNG to output/quod/roof_*.png.\n\nDo not invert the mask: Join Image with Alpha already converts the removal mask to opacity. Use Mask Pen, not RGB Paint Pen.\n\nThis workflow preserves selected pixels; it does not generate missing roof edges or the hidden back surface. A plain black preview is not proof of transparency: inspect the saved PNG in an alpha-aware viewer."
      ]
    }
